{"text":"The causes of hypertension are disease, inflammation, injury, congenital defect, sedentary lifestyle, poor diet, age, family history, high sodium intake, smoking, obesity, alcohol consumption, and stress.","timestamp":1794429026779,"_id":"02VnL2cJ0Aau1EZa"}
{"text":"Plaque is composed of fats, cholesterol, and other substances, including white blood cells.","timestamp":1794429030212,"_id":"0HR9suqDHzvGzkLg"}
{"text":"The cell cycle is controlled by regulatory signals in and out of the cell. S and G phases are controlled by proteins called cyclins. When cells come into contact with each other, they stop growing.     - Normal cells halt at checkpoints.     - Proteins determine the condition of the cell.     - Cells must pass the checkpoints to proceed with cell division.         1. G1 checkpoint             - is cell division necessary?             - is the cell large enough for g2?         1. G2 checkpoint             - was DNA replicated correctly?         1. metaphase checkpoint             - are the chromosomes attached to the microtubules?","timestamp":1794429961100,"_id":"0eJOZqd8e13GdQf5"}
{"text":"An embolism is a blockage in a blood vessel. Typically, it starts as thrombus, breaks free, and floats through the circulatory system and lodges in a small vessel, where it can block blood flow and cause tissue death.","timestamp":1794429004195,"_id":"0vEB7DpqFIE0iFVE"}
{"text":"Nervous system -- vagus nerve bc 95% of serotonin is produced in the gut; immune -- gut-associated lymphoid tissue bc 70% of the immune system resides in the gut & fiber helps train immune cells to be less reactive n inflammed; endocrine -- hunger hormones, affect satiety and weight management.","timestamp":1794428777983,"_id":"15McJBAXiWQNjAzm"}
{"text":"This means that the gut will not have low-grade inflammation and will produce more serotonin...?","timestamp":1794428919509,"_id":"1VRKt5u7QPWPNHXC"}
{"text":"Digestion, DNA replication, destruction of toxins in the liver, hormone production, cell regulation, muscle movement, transporting material around the cell, respiration, signal transduction. When cellular homeostasis is severely disrupted, cells die.","timestamp":1794428369210,"_id":"1cZLEbP5YENEiufQ"}
{"text":"Lots.","timestamp":1794428950928,"_id":"3AD1rw4k0YkteHIM"}
{"text":"That could lead to insulion resistance, diabetes, cardiovascular disease, and obesity.","timestamp":1794428753727,"_id":"3NPpkfVzEFsgnloC"}
{"text":"The three stages of somatic cell division are interphase, mitosis, and cytokinesis.     - interphase: when the cell grows, organelles duplicate, and DNA is copied     - mitosis: when DNA is split equally into two daughter cells, and two nuclei form, but it's still one cell     - cytokinesis: when the parent cell is cleaved in half, forming two new cells.","timestamp":1794429850283,"_id":"561090W8hICNxh6d"}
{"text":"VTA - Ventral Tegmental Area - chemical factory - manufactures dopamine. Nucleus Accumbens - motivation hub - receives dopamine and acts as \"go-button\", triggers cravings. Prefrontal cortex - executive control center - planning, focus, and self-control. Amygdala - emotion tagger - attaches emotional weight to experiences. Hippocampus - memory & map keeper - builds a mental map of how rewards are obtained. Amphetamines cause neurons to release a lot of neurotransmitters or prevent the normal recycling of chemicals.","timestamp":1794429490769,"_id":"5gSzdFpbgQG2LkPx"}
{"text":"The plasma membrane is what bounds the cell. This structure is semipermeable in that it lets some substances through, but not all substances. Hydrophobic substances pass more easily than hydrophilic substances.","timestamp":1794428281498,"_id":"5x5qA8PMCZhxZV67"}
{"text":"A thrombus is a stationary blood clot, either forming along a vessel wall, in the heart, or in the pelvis veins or leg veins, when blood flow is slow.","timestamp":1794428996928,"_id":"6P4IAEO5elpBljI7"}
{"text":"These are produced in the pancreas. Ghrelin is the hunger hormone, leptin is the fullness hormone, and GLP-1s do a lot: support heart health, reduce risk of type 2 diabetes, help with weight loss, lower A1C levels, stimulates insulin release, slows gastic emptying, reduces hunger.","timestamp":1794428794525,"_id":"73fMW7MJbLoXkY1J"}
{"text":"Arteries carry oxygen-rich blood away from the heart, veins carry oxygen-poor blood to the heart, and capillaries🩷 Capillaries contain thin, porous walls to exchange gases to other materials. Capillaries are also the connecting bridges between arteries and veins.","timestamp":1794429167478,"_id":"7EDCCjYtbnDYyPR7"}
{"text":"Sensory neurons carry information toward the CNS from sensory receptors (instead of dendrites). Interneurons, found in the brain and spinal cord, are between sensory and motor neurons. They integrate and interpret sensory signals and account for over 99% of the body's neurons. Motor neurons carry information from the CNS to an effector, either a muscle or a gland.","timestamp":1794429264694,"_id":"7RyLF8qCOSrznNKV"}
{"text":"Water dissolves substances, disperses nutrients, eliminates waste, facilitates metabolism, and moderates body temperature.","timestamp":1794428821775,"_id":"7enptPdkdIWXsjgV"}
{"text":"Minor: cramps, fatigue, headache, dizziness, nausea, confusion, increased heart rate. Major: hallucinations, heat stroke, may result in death.","timestamp":1794428834032,"_id":"7xYSB4Ye1bhRGZSr"}
{"text":"Not enough insulin to regulate blood glucose levels.","timestamp":1794429682190,"_id":"8DNLru87TUFFnvKz"}
{"text":"Target cells do not adequately respond to insulin.","timestamp":1794429688997,"_id":"8z2z5X1NwAukUxLn"}
{"text":"Brain, spinal cord, nerves -- trachea, lung, bronchi -- enables gas exchange to supply blood with oxygen and remove co2.","timestamp":1794428510564,"_id":"9mLKCr3Vi4mEInrn"}
{"text":"The myelin sheath provides electrical insulation that increases the rate of conduction of a nerve impulse. The myelin sheath is made of Schwann cells, which are a type of glial cell. The myelin sheath surrounds the axon. A node of Ranvier is a gap in between Schwann cells. Electrical impulses jump between nodes of Ranvier in a process called saltatory conduction to travel across the body. These nodes of Ranvier speed up the movement of electrical impulses. The autoimmune disease in which the immune system destroys the myelin sheath is Multiple sclerosis.","timestamp":1794429359130,"_id":"A3uVLGWV4I3GcWaS"}
{"text":"Nitrogenous base (adenine), sugar (ribose), 3 negatively charged phosphates. Energy is stored in the chemical bonds between the second and third phosphate.","timestamp":1794428442704,"_id":"AjTDnD75N3PBHhsn"}
{"text":"Senses environment, communicates with and activates other parts of the body.","timestamp":1794428491322,"_id":"AuluA2iKYveaVm9T"}
{"text":"Carcinogens are substances, organisms, or agents capable of causing cancer.","timestamp":1794429823936,"_id":"CNt1Ajhv27mgNRDs"}
{"text":"Esophagus, stomach liver, gallbladder, pancreas, small and large intestines -- ingests and breaks down food so that it can be absorbed by the body.","timestamp":1794428529626,"_id":"CZmJ5noT6QONAfHg"}
{"text":"Epinephrine -- like adrenaline, increase heart rate. Norepinephrine -- also in response to stress, increase blood rate.","timestamp":1794429603617,"_id":"CcR4QMMzyFnDRuyQ"}
{"text":"The hypothalamus is the control center for regulating body temperature. Three effectors are sweat glands, blood vessels in the skin, and skeletal muscles.","timestamp":1794429531833,"_id":"DP4dRR3skQwCb0p1"}
{"text":"Neurons are composed of the dendrites, the cell body, and the axon. The dendrites receive signals from other cells and carry information towards the cell body. The cell body contains the nucleus and other organelles and functions to maintain the neuron. Additionally, the organelles in the cell body make and assemble neurotransmitters that are transported in vesicles to axon endings. The axon carries information away from the cell body to either another neuron or an effector.","timestamp":1794429273657,"_id":"EGdMZnf44BieKmOh"}
{"text":"Kidney, ureter, bladder, urethra -- eliminates liquid wastes; regulates water balance.","timestamp":1794428541684,"_id":"FEnkRSsQToUXTnYS"}
{"text":"Female -- ovary, uterus, cervix, vagina -- produces eggs, supports offspring development. Male -- prostate, testicle, penis -- produces and delivers sperm and associated fluids.","timestamp":1794428562770,"_id":"G3epe4oS1z3iXTGA"}
{"text":"Primary sources are the actual accounts of data or historical events. Secoundary sources reference these primary sources, these actual accounts, for data as opposed to actually having it. Primary journals carry higher credibility because it is direct, first-hand evidence, while secondary sources interpret this data, and may be incorrect.","timestamp":1794428633437,"_id":"G4iKj6DXYc5XDKJt"}
{"text":"Basal Metabolic Rate is the energy use of a resting, wakeful person with an average of 1680 calories a day.","timestamp":1794428380761,"_id":"HPeyCCK0e3SgMhGq"}
{"text":"High temperature and high acidic levels/low pH can denature enzymes.","timestamp":1794428467022,"_id":"HdpxfCXl39fAGCT8"}
{"text":"The phospholipid bilayer has phospholipids with a hydrophilic head and and hydrophobic tail. The hydrophilic head is on the outside of the phospholipid bilayer, the hydrophobic tail facing inwards, and there is another phospholipid whose tail meets the other tail, and its head faces towards the inside of the cell.","timestamp":1794428312520,"_id":"IQCFBBdEUX9cT5Sj"}
{"text":"Health equity is having proper accomodations for different populations to ensure that no one people has statistically worse health outcomes than any other people. Health equity is the attainment of the highest level of health for all people.","timestamp":1794428609238,"_id":"JG6GjymjPQnh35fP"}
{"text":"The nucleus contains DNA, and RNA copies of one of the DNA strands in the nucleus code for a protein. The process of this RNA copy leaving the nucleus is called transcription. Then, ribosomes on the rough ER combine amino acids as coded by the RNA to make a protein.","timestamp":1794429807070,"_id":"JQJIW4XnABCjTMYx"}
{"text":"Glycemic index ranks carbs by how much they raise blood sugar levels after being eaten or drank. A food with a high glycemic index means it spikes your blood sugar levels.","timestamp":1794428748386,"_id":"JWWMwHqo1B0diJLb"}
{"text":"    - Immunotherapy aims to boost the natural immune response against cancer cells via vaccines, which can either be against cancer-causing viruses or stimulate T-cells to attack and kill cancer cells.     - Antiagiogenic therapy is typically used in combination with chemotherapy to inhibit blood vessel formations for blood vessels that nourish and provide a pathway for cancerous cell migration.     - Gene therapy can either be:         - inserting normal tumor-suppressor genes into cancerous cells         - inserting a piece of DNA into a cancer cell that prevents an oncogene from being effective         - inserting a gene into tumor cells that will make them more sensitive to a drug that will kill them.","timestamp":1794430003398,"_id":"JhgdKTXnjpDpGnbY"}
{"text":"The cell nucleus holds hereditary material (DNA), and chromatin is a mix of this DNA and protein.","timestamp":1794428326947,"_id":"KL3TiGw5Ergq4vhL"}
{"text":"Correlational research is research that shows a relationship between two variables, but it is limited because this does not prove that one variable causes the other as opposed to simply being coincidental.","timestamp":1794428672139,"_id":"KnJydjBNopk5eA9Y"}
{"text":"Hypertension is high blood pressure. Physicians mostly consider over a 160/90 mm Hg resting reading to be high enough to require treatment. In that number, 160 refers to the systolic blood pressure, which is the blood pressure during contraction (during a beat), and 90 refers to diastoolic blood pressure, which is the blood pressure between beats.","timestamp":1794429016292,"_id":"LDUa2Dnlf0KnYNHr"}
{"text":"The hypothalamus links the endocrine and nervous systems together. its the structure inthe brain that drives the endocrine system.","timestamp":1794429578866,"_id":"LLnF2csam0Lkk333"}
{"text":"Stem cells in bone marrow give rise to red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets, which are formed elements.","timestamp":1794429052035,"_id":"LSOYV3m4yh9xAV0c"}
{"text":"The systems that help body achieve stability through change (allostasis) in response to physical or psychological stress. eg autonomic nervous system, cardiovascular system.","timestamp":1794429465645,"_id":"MQDEuT4w3kEkQAkg"}
{"text":"Short chain fatty acids: reinforce intestinal cell tight junctions, essential vitamins (K and B-Complex), neurotransmitters, amino acid derivatives, and secondary bile acids.","timestamp":1794428770286,"_id":"NWgwfXXsH8R2uvwp"}
{"text":"Some of the risks of synthetically produced GLP-1s are hair loss and vomiting/nausea. Instead of taking GLP-1s, you can eat foods with lower glycemix indices. Also, synthetic GLP-1s stay in the system for a week. Other stuff: bloating, constipation, pancreatitis, gallbladder edisease, suicidal ideation, thyroid cancer, muscle loss, malnutrition.","timestamp":1794428804060,"_id":"O6ulyt6SACulIDT0"}
{"text":"Red blood cells carry oxygen and contain hemoglobin, which bind to gases, white blood cells defend against disease sometimes via phagocytosis, and platelets are essential to clotting.","timestamp":1794429085277,"_id":"OzZqR41GaxvDKDHK"}
{"text":"Fats form hormones, steroids, and cholesterol; make up the outer membrane of cells; act as energy storage molecules; and act as a cushion and insulator for organs, blood vessels, and nerves.","timestamp":1794428814041,"_id":"PHf1T1i2UWrbVWlj"}
{"text":"The CNS, or the Central Nervous System, consists of the brain and the spinal cord. It integrates incoming information and coordinates with all voluntary and involuntary nervous functions. The PNS, or the Peripheral Nervous System, consists of the ganglia and the nerves that branch from the CNS. It keeps the CNS in contact with the rest of the body.  The PNS is subdivided into the somatic nervous system and the autonomic nervous system. The somatic nervous system receives sensory information and directs voluntary movements, while the autonomic nervous system regulates involuntary activities. The autonomic nervous system subdivides into the sympathetic nervous system and the parasympathetic nervous system. The sympathetic nervous system is fight-or-flight, in charge during emergencies, and the parasympathetic nervous system is #chillmoder awesomesauce normalmode, which adjusts bodily functions during restful times.","timestamp":1794429221016,"_id":"Pom87gTeKz9LmNN5"}
{"text":"A single scientific study is insufficient to confirm a hypothesis because it is unknown whether or not the results can be reproduced, and there may be great bias present in the data or the people conducting the study. Being able to reproduce results increases the reliability of a study. The parameters that must be evaluated when reviewing research are bias, methodology, verifiability, reliability, and reproducibility.","timestamp":1794428639606,"_id":"Pr4zTd24QxglpBXc"}
{"text":"Obesity, diabetes, cardiovascular disease.","timestamp":1794428940477,"_id":"QHPJQPUf3Gtm6gI5"}
{"text":"GG ferkin EZ🤣 Oxygen-poor blood from the cardiovascular system enters the pulmonary circuit, the right side of the heart. Right atrium -> right ventricle -> pulmonary arteries -> capillaries in lungs -> pulmonary veins -> left atrium. Then, starting at the left atrium, this oxygen-rich blood is pumped through the systemic circuit, delivering blood to and from body tissues. Left atrium -> left ventricle -> aorta -> capillaries in blood tissues -> superior and inferior vena cava -> right atrium.","timestamp":1794429096293,"_id":"QOUq1RboY3RAylnC"}
{"text":"Systolic blood pressure is the top number -- the amount of pressure in the arteries during contraction. Diastolic blood pressure is the bottom number -- the amount of pressure in the arteries at rest, between beats. Knowing this is important because there is an acceptable range to be in, otherwise you could have hypertension or hypotension. Above 160/90 mm Hg is high and requires treatment. Hypertension can cause aneurysms, which are dilations or bulges in blood vessels.","timestamp":1794429206757,"_id":"QUuMKAXs9T4n2PGV"}
{"text":"The two major cells of the nervous system are the neuron, or the nerve cell, and the neuroglial cell, or the glial cell. The neurons generate and transmit messages, while the glial cells provide structural support, growth factors, and insulating sheaths around axons. Neuroglial cells outnumber neurons 10:1, and there are several types of neuroglial cells.","timestamp":1794429248139,"_id":"QVYVxP6lafthgy2J"}
{"text":"Activate neurons because their structures mimic natural neurotransmitters. Cause neurons to release a lot of natural neurotransmitters. Prevent the normal recycling of of brain chemicals by disrupting normal communication.","timestamp":1794429507787,"_id":"SAOkEshKnAignYa8"}
{"text":"Blood clots occur when plaque builds up in an artery and the plaque ruptures, causing platelets and immune factors to rush in, potentially clotting and preventing blood flow through the vessel. ","timestamp":1794428992473,"_id":"SOLXT3wTAAa657S9"}
{"text":"The 5 macronutrients are protein, carbs, fiber, fats/lipids, and water.","timestamp":1794428720728,"_id":"TGLZewVvbxRJuboz"}
{"text":"Protects against infections -- thymus, lymph nodes, lymphatic vessels, spleen.","timestamp":1794428521433,"_id":"TkE4vqz1nSG1uAP4"}
{"text":"A heart attack occurs when there is diminished blood flow to the heart muscle, starving it of oxygen.","timestamp":1794428976895,"_id":"TlbxX3w0k2BRLHe7"}
{"text":"Hormonal disruption -- alters cortisol levels.","timestamp":1794429674693,"_id":"Tu7JkP3MSVdZkeyz"}
{"text":"Chromosomes, located in the nucleus, are tightly coiled combinations of DNA molecules and histones (specialized proteins). There are 46 chromosomes in a human somatic cell.","timestamp":1794429827721,"_id":"TupbbC3MhYkQDRF1"}
{"text":"Cortisol maintains blood sugar by converting them to glucose, maintains constant blood pressure, and regulates metabolism.","timestamp":1794429611900,"_id":"Twd4D0IfPwuk1rXw"}
{"text":"Both benign and malignant tumors are abnormal growths in cells. A benign tumor is an abnormal mass of tissue surrounded by a capsule of connective tissue that resembles other tissue cells, usually remains at the site where it forms, and often can be completely removed by surgery. A malignant tumor no longer resembles the surrounding tissue cells, invades surrounding tissue, spreads to multiple locations (this is called metastasis), and is cancerous.","timestamp":1794429835335,"_id":"UFx5m4rPYkvYQAzi"}
{"text":"Social functioning is the ability of a person to participate in and contribute to society. Some environmental factors that can hinder it are lack of education, family environment, poverty, and air quality.","timestamp":1794428580012,"_id":"UUV7v7aXHSExr1b7"}
{"text":"Metabolism is all of the chemical reactions happening in the body at any time. Enzymes are proteins that catalyze and regulate the rates of metabolic reactions. They work with the substrates by binding to it so it fits snugly in the active site, stressing and splitting the substrate's bonds, to release two subunits. Also enzymes lower the activation energy.","timestamp":1794428342564,"_id":"VtGKElekoy7I3VWw"}
{"text":"Acute - hyperglycemia, hypoglycemia, diabetic ketoacidosis. Long-term - high blood glucose damages blood vessels, infections of the skin and gums, depression.","timestamp":1794429728012,"_id":"W6aXbrAA6W50vHdc"}
{"text":"Primarily, the endocrine system and nervous system are responsible for the communication and maintenance of homeostasis.","timestamp":1794429521720,"_id":"WBD17l8q4JmsPiTa"}
{"text":"    The three stages of interphase are G1, S, and G2.     - G1: cell grows, organelles duplicate     - S: DNA replicates     - G2: cell makes proteins needed to complete mitosis.","timestamp":1794429859808,"_id":"XFWN58kacsh6moMD"}
{"text":"Coronary artery disease entails fatty deposits of atherosclerosis occuring in the coronary arteries that are supposed to supply the heart muscle. It is the underlying cause of most heart attacks, and it is signified by chest pain (angina pectoris).","timestamp":1794429010634,"_id":"XIy3tugIZFK3Dlfi"}
{"text":"Nutrients are substances in food that sustain life, health, growth, and provide structural materials and energy for the body.","timestamp":1794428708554,"_id":"XwVwaspAOFUTjICJ"}
{"text":"Vitamins act as co-enzymes for metabolic reactions.","timestamp":1794428895678,"_id":"XwidZNHHKrr2qM3a"}
{"text":"Blood is composed of plasma (about 55% )and formed elements (about 45%). Plasma is ~93% water and ~7% dissolved substances (ions, dissolved gases, hormones, plasma proteins, waste products). Formed elements are cellular components e.g. red blood cells (oxygen transport), white blood cells (disease defense), and platelets (essential for clotting). Stem cells in bone marrow give rise to formed elements.","timestamp":1794429047480,"_id":"YfWdsgA44DcvJq92"}
{"text":"Food deserts & swamps, economic disparities, and targeted marketing.","timestamp":1794428933373,"_id":"YpzZOUnv70Pza1aQ"}
{"text":"Coronary circulation nourishes the heart muscle. Coronary arteries, which are the first two arteries that branch off the aorta and branch extensively, bring oxygen and nutrients to the heart muscle. Coronary veins get blood through capillary beds and has them flow into the right atrium.","timestamp":1794429198879,"_id":"ZFmosJDNRZC0G49M"}
{"text":"Increased calcium will prevent iron from being absorbed by the intestines.","timestamp":1794428906146,"_id":"ZJhw8KcmS6ZLvMVp"}
{"text":"    - Surgery         - performed when the tumor is accessible and can be removed without damaging vital tissue.         - complete cure possible with early tumors         - if cancer has spread, then other forms of treatment may be necessary.     - radiation         - used when cancer has spread from initial site but is still localized         - typically follows surgery.     - chemotherapy         - used when cancer has spread at diagnosis         - drugs carried by the circulatory system         - used to kill rapidly dividing cells throughout the body.","timestamp":1794429973216,"_id":"aNHnQdoisQD9V39h"}
{"text":"Homeostasis is the process of the body ensuring its internal state is proper to function.","timestamp":1794428456665,"_id":"amF2K3NlLozCqq6g"}
{"text":"An organ is a group of two or more tissue types that work together to perform a specific function, and an organ system is a group of organs that work together.","timestamp":1794428478654,"_id":"b947r7VmRCWD6cY4"}
{"text":"Homeostasis is the ability to maintain a consistent internal environment under changing conditions. Three internal conditions that the human body must maintain are temperature, heart rate, and water/mineral balance.","timestamp":1794429515886,"_id":"bvWPUtafGp1abrrG"}
{"text":"Health literacy is the set of skills needed to function effectively in the health care environment. This includes reading medical text, measuring blood and glocuse levels, and other stuff. The seven concrete steps: check source, examine author credentials, pay attention to date, cross-reference, question sensational claims, evidence > anecdotes, talk with professionals, when in doubt do not share.","timestamp":1794428679721,"_id":"cL9TJ1qGWGOVQw1e"}
{"text":"80-130 mg/dl before meals and below 180 mg/dl after meals.","timestamp":1794429751477,"_id":"cNwggDfIimSWjCrA"}
{"text":"All living things: are made of cells, have DNA/RNA, undergo metabolic reactions, grow and reproduce, respond to external stimuli, and maintain homeostasis.","timestamp":1794429801666,"_id":"cZO10wkKvEZgA5gv"}
{"text":"The axon of a nerve cell has repeating units of sodium channels, potassium channels, and sodium/potassium pumps. When a neuron is not conducting a nerve impulse, it is at rest / resting potential. The inner surface of the membrane is at -70mV. There are more sodium ions on the outside than the inside, and there are more potassium ions on the inside than the outside. During resting potential, the sodium channels and the potassium channels are closed. When -50mV is reached, depolarization starts, in which sodium channels open and allow sodium to flow inside of the cell. This happens until 30mV is hit, where the sodium channel closes and the potassium channel opens, allowing potassium to flow out of the cell to make it negative again in a process called repolarization. The plasma membrane is responsible for reaching threshold. The action potential travels across the axon.","timestamp":1794429389340,"_id":"cw7RS6vdrU9Zlw85"}
{"text":"This simply means that vitamins are carbon-based.","timestamp":1794428901381,"_id":"dcuLuvwcoqF9DqAc"}
{"text":"A codon is a three-nucleotide sequence in and RNA or DNA strand.","timestamp":1794429811107,"_id":"eLDnfrf8RxWzUDWb"}
{"text":"Historical redlining was the labelling of certain neighborhoods as unsafe and having people of color present, so that people would not invest in these neighborhoods, which led to these neighborhoods being deprived of resources and public goods. This proves that racism is a systemic issue. This historical lack of investment has led to some neighborhoods not having the same resources as other neighborhoods, which has led to more impoverished regions and populations. Class is a social determinent of health, and it is known that financially burdened families will choose unhealthy food, which has definitely made it so that access to cheap, unhealthy food is more prominent than healthy, nutricious food. This can lead to obesity and diabetes.","timestamp":1794428616799,"_id":"eygYF4KGQHUB8fxw"}
{"text":"An aneurysm is a localized, abnormal dilation or bulging of a blood vessel, caused by a weakening of the vessel wall. It can be asymptomatic, but it carries the risk of blood clots or blood loss due to bursting.","timestamp":1794429021117,"_id":"f49ylgnnv08WBdBz"}
{"text":"Three risk factors for cancer development are drinking, smoking, and wood dust.","timestamp":1794429840156,"_id":"fG8F1hGxhQTy1VuC"}
{"text":"Proteins are necessary to regulate processes in cells and bodies (enzymes) and providing energy if needed if fats and carbs are not present.","timestamp":1794428809353,"_id":"fY1Kze2tZMhRMpM5"}
{"text":"Cardiovascular disease prevention can entail reducing risk factors, such as being more active, having a lower-sodium diet of whole, nutricious foods, avoiding smoking, maintaining a healthy weight, avoiding alcohol, and avoiding stress.","timestamp":1794429034460,"_id":"gQftbjhliERyhgx8"}
{"text":"Water-soluble vitamins are toxic when taken in excess. Fat-soluble vitamins dissolve in fat, while water-soluble vitamins dissolve in water.","timestamp":1794428743834,"_id":"ggNTmF3hILQS2YU4"}
{"text":"The three fundamental structural root causes of health inequities, according to public health frameworks, are race/ethnicity, gender/sexuality, & financial status.","timestamp":1794428622330,"_id":"hHuPhFQnCrq6B6Am"}
{"text":"Glutamate - excitatory; most abundant in brain; important for thinking, learning, and memory; imbalances linked with alzheimers, dementia, parkinsons, and seizures. GABA - most common inhibitory in brain; regulates brain activity to prevent problems with anxiety, irritability, concentration, sleep, seizures, and depression. Acetylcholine - acts in both PNS and CNS; released at motor neurons; activates muscles. Serotonin - promotes well-being; influences mood, sleep, digestion, would healing, sexual desire, and body temp. Dopamine - regulates emotion, memory, pleasure reward/motivation, behavior and cognition, attention, sleep and arousal, learning, lactation, and compex movements.","timestamp":1794429457208,"_id":"iAWpRM88S0IhQOfP"}
{"text":"Cells divide for the purpose of growth, development, and repair.","timestamp":1794429815205,"_id":"imLZmSYp56oINkCs"}
{"text":"Blood vessels, heart -- enables transport of nutrients, gases, hormones, and wastes to and from the cells of the body.","timestamp":1794428500835,"_id":"jOLpIqXO2qWsxwEv"}
{"text":"We can make sure to second-guess influencers, listen to our doctors, and look at research online.","timestamp":1794428963620,"_id":"jPrjWK3qXK9lqHeb"}
