{"text":"The fluid mosaic model describes how lipids and proteins are able to move about within the inside of the plasma membrane.","timestamp":1794428320397,"_id":"kypJxi6LmuN570Zb"}
{"text":"Glycated hemoglobin a1c measures the percentage of hemoglobin molecules that have glucose attached and indicates the blood glucose for the past month, while fasting is after overnight fast.","timestamp":1794429735946,"_id":"l1j3yst3nVYMQ2rr"}
{"text":"The micronutrients are vitamins and minerals.","timestamp":1794428729217,"_id":"mk7ClPYYDFB3wUBT"}
{"text":"Social determinants of health are non-medical factors that affect one's health outcomes. The five structural domains outlined in public health frameworks are education access/quality, healthcare access/quality, economic stability, neighborhood/built environment, and social/community context.","timestamp":1794428586103,"_id":"mnqepdEtEhrBVrvq"}
{"text":"Five capitalist commercial industries whose products can negatively impact public health are tech, alcohol, weed, junk food, and gambling. Predatory marketing can affect social work interventions by getting people addicted to the products of these industries, or by costing people money and keeping them impoverished. The gambling especially exemplifies this, by using intermittent reinforcement to keep people addicted while draining them of their money.","timestamp":1794428627931,"_id":"muzHvAXxB1Go0FpN"}
{"text":"Man-made or natural substances that interfere with the endocrine system.","timestamp":1794429654848,"_id":"nyB1Ao4vKFjk6vvR"}
{"text":"Right atrium - upper, smaller, and thin-walled. Left atrium -  upper, smaller, and thin-walled. Right ventricle - lower, larger, and more muscular. Left ventricle -  lower, larger, and more muscular. Right side has deoxygenated blood which has to go to the lungs. Left side has oxygenated blodo which has to go to the body.","timestamp":1794429192934,"_id":"oDo1F8muB41BkcE4"}
{"text":"Prophase chromosomes condense nuclear envelope disappears microtubules attach to centrioles at the poles of each cell and pull the chromosomes around. Metaphase chromosomes align across the middle of the cell by microtubules. Anaphase centromeres split sister chromatids are pulled apart towards opposite poles. Telophase nuclear envelopes reform around chromosomes chromosomes revert to uncondensed form.","timestamp":1794429945024,"_id":"odDqiW4OD6Xg7DAD"}
{"text":"Mortality rates are the ratio of people dying to people having a disease or condition.","timestamp":1794428603960,"_id":"p03sVLuDBcPhAANu"}
{"text":"The cell is the basic unit of human life, and organelles all have different functions within the cell. Organelles are groups of similar/identical cells that serve similar/the same function.","timestamp":1794428253671,"_id":"pdh3ktCkI8aD9mCF"}
{"text":"Regulate water balkance by increasing water reabsorption in the kidneys and reducing urine output.","timestamp":1794429636385,"_id":"q17nvPXSmrhLUemN"}
{"text":"Hypothalamic-pituitary adrenal axis (HPA axis) and the sympathetoc-adrenal-medullary axis (SAM axis).","timestamp":1794429667173,"_id":"qAnLFefF9uCmTUaX"}
{"text":"The endocrine system is the internal system of chemical signals involving hormones, the organs and glands that produce/secrete them, and the target cells that respond to them. hormones released by this system interact with target cells in a lock and key model, with target cells being the locks and hormones being the key. hormones are either lipid-based or water-based.","timestamp":1794429562133,"_id":"qJL7YLRi8zcT8IgJ"}
{"text":"Pituitary gland, thyroid/parathyroid, thymus -- secretes hormones into bloodstream.","timestamp":1794428551693,"_id":"qgryQ8W6tIqL5fC9"}
{"text":"Aerobic cellular respiration occurs in the mitochondria and requires oxygen. It converts glucose and oxygen to ATP in the mitochondria. Oxygen is attained through the respiratory system, and glucose is obtained through breaking down carbohydrates in the digestive system.","timestamp":1794428450496,"_id":"qpvSMipyUquBRzck"}
{"text":"Temporary sterility, nausea, anemia, hair loss.","timestamp":1794429983821,"_id":"qyiaiIjHuvFNxPYO"}
{"text":"Ultra processed foods are foods entirely constructed from substances made from other foods, instead of the base foods themselves.","timestamp":1794428911884,"_id":"rYdW5CMCRcwAr3ES"}
{"text":"The human body needs macronutrients in large amounts, in grams daily, while the human body needs micronutrients in small amounts, in milligrams or micrograms daily.","timestamp":1794428713449,"_id":"rZ4uCOcucxf3yIpq"}
{"text":"Co-enzymes are enzymes that work together with the substrate to lower the activation energy of a metabolic process.","timestamp":1794428472708,"_id":"rqzcJQWhXwJt6Cvt"}
{"text":"The nerve impulse reaches the synaptic knob of the presynaptic neuron. Calcium ions move into the synaptic knob which releases the neurotransmitter into the synaptic cleft through exocytosis. The neurotransmitter diffuses across the synaptic cleft and binds with receptors on the membrane of the dendrites of the postsynaptic neuron, causing an ion channel to open.","timestamp":1794429404913,"_id":"sNieK8ImD6VRaDBc"}
{"text":"Atherosclerosis is the process of narrowing the lumen of the blood vessel, caused by the deposition of plaque (fats, cholesterol, and other substances).","timestamp":1794428985561,"_id":"tBzzIWEWtQQAVvMw"}
{"text":"Condition in which pregnant women develop diabetes mellitus when the placenta produces hormones that make the mother's cells more resistant to insulin and her production of insulin is insufficient to overcome this resistance.","timestamp":1794429745234,"_id":"tDRMbCo2T4jyQmnc"}
{"text":"Negative feedback mechanisms primarily maintain homeostasis. Negative feedback mechanisms indicate that the product of a process inhibits the process, while positive feedback mechanisms indicate that the product of a process promotes the process.","timestamp":1794429526682,"_id":"tRNGTV4EOwaOCysk"}
{"text":"Active reuptake by presynaptic terminal pump. Diffusion back into presynaptic terminal. Deactivation by enzymes.","timestamp":1794429427992,"_id":"tlcEAYzwP2Z3uCPu"}
{"text":"The cellular basis for cancer is uncontrolled cell division.","timestamp":1794429780305,"_id":"u6n0bJTaEDXiolPo"}
{"text":"Prior to cell division, all internal contents have to be duplicated including the chromosomes and nucleus so that the new cell will have the exact same structures and information.","timestamp":1794429819667,"_id":"vdQYv77fFaM7GWXi"}
{"text":"The mitochondria's primary biological function is to produce ATP.","timestamp":1794428335306,"_id":"vfCPVMJSYTZZ93aK"}
{"text":"Soluble fiber dissolves in water to form a gel, which lowers LDL cholesterol and regulates blood glucose levels, and insoluble fiber adds \"bulk\" to stool and promotes peristalsis, preventing constipation and diverticulosis. Diverticulosis is low-grade inflammation of the colon.","timestamp":1794428760074,"_id":"wu0lu7GfxsBnmfZf"}
{"text":"Activation energy is the amount of energy needed for a metabolic reaction, and enzymes lower the activation energy to facilitate reactions and reduce time required for reactions to commence.","timestamp":1794428350442,"_id":"xGRFW2uyRbvoVBXu"}
{"text":"Chronic diseases are diseases that remain dormant in your body and flare up occasionally, as opposed to being something that is contracted once and then lost. Some major examples tracked in health equity reports are like i dont fucking know i guess obesity and diabetes in relationship to access to healthy, nutritious food.","timestamp":1794428595180,"_id":"yPkNMro0CxPUwRTx"}
{"text":"Blood functions as a transportation system; as protection against disease, mayhaps in the form of clotting; and to maintain homeostasis of pH and temperature. As a **transportation system**, the distribution of blood delivers oxygen and nutrients to cells, while also removing waste and delivering it to other systems to be eliminated from the body. Pulmonary arteries deliver oxygen-poor blood to the lungs, pulmonary veins deliver oxygen-rich blood from the lungs to the heart, and coronary arteries delivery blood to the heart muscle. As **protection**, the body removes wastes, toxins, and damaged and abnormal cells, as well as helping the body defend against disease: Blood can leave the circulatory system and travel to sites of infection or tissue damage, and some white blood cells can even perform phagocytosis, which is when blood cells 'eat' harmful particles by engulfing them in their plasma membranes. As **homeostasis maintenance**, the blood regulates temperature and pH.","timestamp":1794429041443,"_id":"yZjCxrGS4mo8gz1l"}
{"text":"Social work is the practice of working with disenfranchised/marginalized groups to better their quality of life. Micro means working with just one person, mezzo means working with a small group, such as a school, and macro means a large group, like policy & governmental systems.","timestamp":1794428573198,"_id":"ycWPySgQsh0csUmz"}
{"text":"The cerebrum controls language, memory, voluntary movements, sensations, and decision-making. The thalamus is the relay center for sensory information and motor response to the cerebrum. The hypothalamus is the control center for sex drive, pleasure, pain, hunger, thirst, blood pressure, and body temperature. The cerebellum is responsible for balance, muscle movement, and coordination. The brain stem governs reflexes, heartbeat, breathing, swallowing, and other autonomic functions.","timestamp":1794429213487,"_id":"z3RQMyf3HOJnFTmg"}
